    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0892" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3923: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Conservative Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Meneses</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and the Secretary
                        of the Liberal Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Camorales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at the Corinto Conference to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>U. S. S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Denver</hi>”</placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1926-10-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received October 18, 1926—11:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>At the inauguration of the peace conferences on board the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Denver</hi> both delegations send Your Excellency their respects and hope
                    that under the friendly offices of the American Government peace will be
                    restored.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Barcenas Meneses</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Camorales</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
